  through and WRITES, against `dbErrors.ts`'s own KS-253 doc comment) is an open call for Wednesday / KS-1018 item 3.
  A 404-only pin would red on an F4 fix; this one was measured green on the propagate shape (P6, F4-neutral row). If
  Wednesday rules F4 "fall-through stays", tightening to 404 is a one-line follow-up.
- **What the pin couples.** Answering a query-level error on the review read with 503, or writing anything on that
  path, now edits this file too. The fragment `WHERE id = ` is read from the review SELECT: rewording it reddens the 🟢
  control, which is the intended alarm.
